# One canonical line ending, everywhere.
#
# This repo is edited from Windows IDEs, Linux shells, and agents running in
# containers. Without a rule, each of those writes its own ending and every file
# churns wholesale between them — which matters more here than usual: a pull
# request whose every line reads as changed cannot be reviewed, and human review
# is the scarce resource this whole pipeline is built around.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than the more common bare `text=auto`: normalizing in the repo
# but checking out native still leaves Windows working copies in CRLF, so any
# tool that writes LF re-dirties the file. One form in the repo and in every
# working copy removes the translation step entirely. Modern editors on Windows
# handle LF without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated: collapse the diff and keep it out of language statistics. The
# content is real and committed, but nobody reviews it line by line.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff

# Never translate these — a byte changed is a file corrupted. Design assets
# (screens, exported mockups) are pipeline evidence and will eventually be
# tracked even though today they sit under a gitignored examples/ directory.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
